Z||000000||GILLICK||06-17-2001||09:09 PM||||I have searched the snot out of this topic and would love a clarification by anyone.  Peferably by someone who knows what they are talking about, but I will listen to B.S. too!  LMAO.  These are the size wheels I am contemplating on using;<P>Front:<BR>       2" drop spindles<BR>       17 x 7.0 40mm offset<BR>       215 40 17<P>Rear:<BR>       Coilovers<BR>       18 x 7.5 45mm offset<BR>       245 40 18<P><BR>Does anyone see any complications with this setup?<P>Will these offsets make the wheels stay too far inboard (vs. the stock 35mm)?  It seems to me if stock wheels are 15x7 35mm then a wheel of the same width with a larger offset will result in the wheels being further inboard?<P>Lastly, will these size tires fit well?<P><BR>Thanks in advance for any and all replies.  Fiero fans are truly the most cooperative and helpful out of any car folk that I have ever met (chatted).<P><BR> <P>------------------<BR>John D. Gillick<BR>jgillick@swbell.net||||reg||1
Z||000001||TRiAD||06-17-2001||09:14 PM||||Yo John, what engine are you running?<P>If you by chance are lucky enough to have a V8 swap (or BIg power equivilent) I would consider <I>smaller</I> diameter wheels in the rear, allowing more sidewall, but a more compliant rear, and more sidewall "flex" at launch, for better hookup. <P>If yer running the 200hp max stock setup, you can comletely disregard my senseless ramblings.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Sorry I have no info on your real question, but I'll be reading the other replies with great interest...<P>------------------<BR><B><I>Michael ~ triadtuning@hotmail.com</I></B><BR>-----------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88FieroGTwhitefscustomcroppedmini.jpg"> <BR><I>Photoshop rendering of planned exterior modifications.</I>||||reg||1
